WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:09.015
The Dumbbell Nebula is a planetary nebula in the constellation Vulpecula, at a distance of about 1360 light-years.

00:09.478 --> 00:15.033
It was the first such nebula to be discovered, by Charles Messier in 1764.

00:15.661 --> 00:28.014
At its brightness of visual magnitude 7.5 and diameter of about 8 arcminutes, it is easily visible in binoculars and is a popular observing target in amateur telescopes.
